      "type": "h1",
      "text": "CSS Responsive Modal Images"
    },
    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Responsive Modal Image Gallery"
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "A modal image gives a user the ability to display a larger version of an\nimage, without navigating away from the current page. When a user clicks on a\nmodal image, it shows a popup window that appears on top of the main content of\nthe webpage, often with a semi-transparent background. The modal must be closed\nby the user, typically with a \"close\" button or an \"X\" sign in top-right corner."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "This example demonstrates how to use HTML, CSS and JavaScript together, to create a responsive modal image gallery."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "We use CSS to create a modal window (dialog box), and hide it by default."
    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "text": "Then, we use a JavaScript to show the modal window with the correct image inside, when a user clicks on the image:"
    },
